# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Jiuyang Liang et al. (2026). Prolate spheroidal wave functions enable fast and exponent-aware long-range machine learning interatomic potentials.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2606.06617  arXiv:2606.06617v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2606.06617v1 (sha256 bf100acea0d36771...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 661 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/liang2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the PSWF-LR models introduced in the paper (registry
# method PSWF-LR, origin) on the five nonlocal charge-transfer benchmarks
# of Table 1 (published data sets), with their test RMSEs. Literature
# baselines in Table 1 (charge-constrained ACE, 3G/4G-HDNNP, CACE-LR,
# NequIP-LR) are taken from other papers and are not encoded. Random
# particle, dimer and dipeptide experiments and PME runtime comparisons are
# shown in figures.

